<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramon Berenguer IV, Count of Barcelona</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1114–<a href="/years/1162">1162</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Ramon Berenguer IV of Barcelona</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramon Berenguer IV was Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> from 1131. His betrothal in 1137 to Petronilla, heiress of Aragon, joined Aragon and Catalonia in the dynastic union later called the Crown of Aragon. He took part in the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a> in 1147 and conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tortosa">Tortosa</a> in 1148 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Lleida</a> in 1149, pushing the frontier down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramon-berenguer-iv-count-of-barcelona.jpg" alt="Ramon Berenguer IV, Count of Barcelona" width="320" height="276" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RB4_1140.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
